&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Celonis is the global leader in Process Intelligence and the pioneer of Process Mining technology. As one of the world’s fastest-growing enterprise SaaS companies, we are changemakers pushing the boundaries of what’s possible. We invest heavily in advanced AI capabilities—specifically our Process Intelligence Graph—to turn data insights into immediate business action. We believe there is a massive opportunity to unlock global productivity and sustainability by placing intelligence at the core of every business process. Join our mission to make processes work for people, companies, and the planet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Celonis Ecosystem team is building and scaling the right partnerships with Tech, Cloud, AI, and Professional Services firms to fuel Celonis’ growth in non-linear ways. Within the Ecosystem, the Strategy Consulting team has a dedicated focus on expanding our collaboration with Strategy Consulting firms through joint business opportunities that are delivering superior client value. We are hiring for a Director - Strategy Consulting Partnerships to join our team, focus on developing and managing our joint Go-To-Market activities across North America.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;As Director - Strategy Consulting Partnerships, you will be responsible for leading and expanding Celonis’ partnerships with Strategy Consulting firms across North America. Your role involves building strong relationships, fostering trust, and developing a shared understanding of business objectives to define joint solutions, shape transformation programs, and influence key business opportunities. Success will be evaluated based on joint business impact, thought leadership, and the creation of scalable go-to-market strategies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Work you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute a holistic Go-To-Market plan for strategy consulting firms across North America, while actively shaping the global ecosystem priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attract and develop senior relationships with sector-, industry-, and capability leaders, regional heads, and responsible account partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Refine and pitch the value proposition of the Celonis partnership to secure buy-in for joint business development in new strategic areas and markets, maintaining a highly business outcome-focused approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source joint projects and ensure delivery success&lt;/strong&gt; by managing Celonis-powered consulting engagements, aligning expectations with consulting partners, and coordinating across internal Celonis teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed Celonis into partner methodologies and offerings, ensuring Celonis is part of the “toolbox” for digital, operational, and functional transformation practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape joint go-to-market initiatives by aligning consulting-led transformation themes (e.g., cost takeout, supply chain resilience, AI &amp;amp; digital operations) with Celonis’ capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and convert pipeline by collaborating closely with Celonis regional- &amp;amp; sales leadership in activating partners in priority accounts, and guiding C-level pitches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage stakeholders across various Celonis functions, partners, customers &amp;amp; third parties to ensure conversion of joint opportunities and successful delivery of client engagements and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive joint thought leadership and marketing through white-papers, market narratives, and industry insights, and joint events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage regional governance with consulting firms, including regular steering committees, pipeline reviews, and project forecasts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
