&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-12 years of relevant work experience in the area of strategy consulting, ideally paired with first exposure to software sales, business development and/or partner management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen, with a track record of driving commercial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the inner workings of strategy consulting firms: their business model, incentive structures, value propositions, and how they drive enterprise transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and storytelling skills, as well as executive presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of guiding senior consulting partners and C-level client executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong network within the North American strategy consulting ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial attitude with the ability to excite others and build strong relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in fast-paced, high-growth environments with strong self-motivation and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel (10-20%)&lt;/li&gt;
