&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and own sophisticated capacity, utilization, and productivity models to ensure hiring and resource allocation align with the sales pipeline and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, track, and analyze critical B2B SaaS metrics and operational data to optimize margins, delivery costs, and overall financial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead quarterly reviews with GTM executives and develop executive-level dashboards in partner platforms to provide real-time visibility and data-backed recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear frameworks and financial models for complex programs, such as commercial partner agreements, revenue recognition, or marketing attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The qualifications you need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic finance, or corporate finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience specifically supporting GTM organizations (such as Services, CS, Marketing, or Channel/Partners) at a B2B SaaS or technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working alongside executive leadership to align operational execution with financial impacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a quantitative field, with an MBA or CFA considered a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of B2B SaaS unit economics, key metrics, and complex multi-touch attribution or revenue recognition rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced to elite Excel and financial modeling skills, including the ability to build dynamic capacity and utilization models from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with enterprise CRM, business intelligence, and FP&amp;amp;A tools such as Pigment, Salesforce, Workday, Adaptive Insights, Tableau, or PowerBI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional data storytelling and communication skills, enabling you to distill massive data sets into clear, executive-level narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to comfortably navigate ambiguity in a high-growth enterprise environment and constructively challenge senior executives using objective data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
